# gui backend test (needs the Firefox flatpak + bwrap, see test/ffbox; skipped by test/run otherwise): mouse clicks in web
# content (the old known gap: Gecko's content subsurface has an empty input region, the pointer must go to GDK's surface)
# and a <select> dropdown (xdg_popup). Firefox runs in a private profile, without network, on the local test/ffpage.
Window gui
Size 1000x700
Title "Firefox (private profile, local page)"
Run env FFBOX_PAGE=${AUTODEMO_ROOT}/ffpage ${AUTODEMO_ROOT}/ffbox file:///page/page.html
WaitFor title "ff-ready" 90s
WaitFor settle 800ms 30s
Caption "click in web content"
MouseMove 300 190 400
MouseClick
WaitFor title "ff-clicked" 10s
Caption "dropdown popup"
MouseMove 300 340 400
MouseClick
WaitFor settle 800ms 10s
MouseMove 161 497 300
MouseClick
WaitFor title "ff-select=two" 10s
Sleep 500ms
